 "about": "Month wallpapers cut from the calendar folios (1v-12v) of the Tres Riches Heures du duc de Berry, Chantilly, Musee Conde MS 65. Each month has one 16:10 background plate (the full width of the miniature inside its frame, a band of it, no parchment) and a few cut-out character layers detected with Apple Vision (VNGenerateForegroundInstanceMaskRequest / VNGeneratePersonInstanceMaskRequest). Layer x/y/width/height are pixels of the background plate; each layer sits exactly on top of the same pixels in the plate, so it can be lifted above page content with z-index without any visible change. focus is the point of the plate that stage.js keeps in view and decides how far the characters at the edges reach into a centred 800 px window. Sources and licence: see credits.json (public domain).",
